// P3B.3 / A14.1–A14.5, X10 (J, H): showing mates in the view, on the mates stand-in
// (`fixtures/mates_standin.cadrs`) with three mates: Planar 1 (Table–Puck), Ball 1
// (Socket–Ball) and Parallel 1 (Table–Magnet).
// 01 (A14.1) mates hidden by default: no mate glyphs; the rows grey.
// 02 (A14.1) J: every mate shown (glyph and type badge at its connector); the rows dark.
// 03 J again: all hidden.
// 04 (A14.2) the eye on Ball 1's row: that mate alone shown.
// 05 (A14.2) hovering Planar 1's row: its instances highlighted and its glyph shown.
// 06 (A14.3) instance menu on the Puck: Show mates / Hide mates.
// 07 Show mates on the Puck: Planar 1 shown too.
// 08 (A14.4) H: show mates mode (the chip); everything hidden again with J, the Socket hovered:
//    its mate shows.
// 09 (A14.4) the Socket clicked (pinned), the pointer moved away: its mate stays shown.
// 10 (A14.5) clicking the Ball mate's badge in the view: its row highlighted in the list.
// 11 (A14.5) right-clicking the badge: the mate menu, with Edit…; 11b Expand ▸ Mate connectors.
Scenario(
    start: Some("document"),
    steps: [
        Wait(10),
        Custom("fixture mates_standin"),
        Wait(10),
        Click(ui("insert-tab")),
        WaitFor("create-assembly"),
        Click(ui("create-assembly")),
        Wait(5),
        Click(ui("insert")),
        WaitFor("insert-dialog"),
        Wait(5),
        Click(ui("insert-search-field")),
        Key("Ctrl+A"),
        Type("Table"),
        Wait(5),
        Click(ui("insert-part-table")),
        Wait(3),
        Click(ui("insert-search-field")),
        Key("Ctrl+A"),
